.TH DIDLC 1 2026-10-25 DarqOS "DarqOS User's Manual"
.SH NAME
didlc \- compile DarqOS interface definitions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B didlc
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.I input
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B didlc
compiles a Darq Interface Definition Language (DIDL) file into an
intermediate representation (IR), written as JSON.
The IR gives the exact byte layout of the body of every request and
response message the file defines, for use by code generators.
It carries a format version number, which is incremented whenever the
IR changes in a way that breaks its consumers.
.SS Language
A DIDL file names a library, and declares enums, structs and
protocols:
.PP
.RS
.nf
library filesystem;

enum Status : uint32 {
    OK = 0;
    NOT_FOUND = 1;
}

struct FileAttributes {
    uint64 size;
    uint32 permissions;
    uint32 owner_id;
}

protocol FileServer {
    1: GetAttributes(uint64 fd) -> (FileAttributes attr, Status status);
    2: Close(uint64 fd);
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each method in a protocol has a request, and optionally a response
introduced by
.BR \-> .
A method without a response is one-way.
.PP
Each method must be given a number, from 1 to 65535, which is carried
in the message header to identify it.
Numbers are assigned by hand, and must be unique within a protocol.
.PP
An enum names a set of integer values, and is based on an integer type
.RB ( int8
to
.BR uint64 ),
which sets its size and alignment in a message.
Each member's value must fit the base type, and be unique within the
enum.
.PP
Numbers are decimal, or hexadecimal with a
.B 0x
prefix, and may be negative.
.PP
Comments start with
.B //
and run to the end of the line.
.SS Types
.TP
.BR bool ", " int8 ", " uint8
1 byte.
.TP
.BR int16 ", " uint16
2 bytes.
.TP
.BR int32 ", " uint32 ", " real32
4 bytes.
.TP
.BR int64 ", " uint64 ", " real64
8 bytes.
.TP
.B opaque
A sequence of bytes.
In the message, an 8-byte, 4-byte aligned descriptor: a
.B uint32
offset and a
.B uint32
length.
The bytes themselves are appended to the end of the message.
.TP
.B string
UTF-8 text, laid out and encoded as an
.BR opaque .
.TP
.BI sequence< type >
A sequence of elements of any type, including other sequences: for
example,
.BR sequence<string> .
In the message, an 8-byte, 4-byte aligned descriptor: a
.B uint32
offset and a
.B uint32
count of elements.
The elements are appended to the end of the message, as an array at a
stride of the element type's size.
The element type can't be an empty struct.
In the IR, a sequence field, and a sequence element, have an
.B element
giving the element type, its size and its alignment.
.TP
.B port
2-byte index into the list of handles transferred with the message,
or 0xFFFF for no port.
A message can transfer at most 64 handles.
.PP
A struct or enum may be used as a field type, before or after its
declaration, but a struct may not contain itself, even in a
sequence.
Enum and struct names must be distinct, and not the names of
primitive types.
.SS Layout
Fields are laid out in order, following the C/C++ ABI: each field is
aligned to its natural boundary, a struct is aligned to its most
strictly aligned member, and every struct and message body is padded
to a multiple of its alignment.
.PP
Every message starts with a fixed 8-byte header, defined by
.B darq.dipc
rather than recorded in the IR; the body follows it:
.TP
.B txid
.BR uint32 :
transaction identifier matching a reply to its request; 0 for one-way
messages.
.TP
.B flags
.BR uint16 :
bit 0 marks an error reply (see
.BR darq.dipc.ErrorReply );
the others are reserved, and must be 0.
.TP
.B method
.BR uint16 :
the method number.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output\fR, " \-\-output " output"
Write the IR to
.IR output ,
or to standard output if
.I output
is
.BR \- .
By default, it is written next to
.IR input ,
with the extension replaced by
.IR .dir .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if the input can't be read or contains an error;
2 if the command line is invalid.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors are reported on standard error as
.PP
.RS
.IB file : line : column ": error: " message
.RE
.PP
and no output file is written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR didlpygen (1),
DarqOS documentation,
.IR doc/ipc.rst .
